OL,3,GNEWSAAutism Guernsey secures #100,000
OL,4,Afunding boost
OL,5,
OL,6,FAutism Guernsey has secured #100,000
OL,7,Ffrom BBC Children in Need, giving the
OL,8,Fcharity funding for the next three
OL,9,Fyears after losing a government grant
OL,10,Fin 2024.
OL,12,FThe charity said the money would fund
OL,13,Fnew support programmes aimed at helping
OL,14,Fautistic children manage anxiety.
OL,16,FChair Andrew Warren said: "We're
OL,17,Fdelighted. It's going to enable us to
OL,18,Fdo some stuff that we've been wanting
OL,19,Fto do for a while, but just haven't had
OL,20,Fthe funds and other resources to do."
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
